# Copy to .env at the repo root (git-ignored) and fill in. Never commit .env, and never prefix these with VITE_:
# a VITE_ variable is written into the browser bundle. The dev server reads them (vite.config.ts) and adds them
# to the vendor calls itself — see docs/data-feed.md. Restart `npm run dev` after a change; `npm run feed:check`
# says whether they work.

# Unusual Whales, API Basic — sent as "Authorization: Bearer …"
UW_API_TOKEN=

# Massive (Polygon), Basic — OFF since 2026-10-14 (Theta Data in its place); nothing reads it
# MASSIVE_API_KEY=

# Theta Data (2026-10-14) — in Massive's place. Handed to the Theta Terminal on this machine when it starts
# (npm run theta:terminal — Java 21), never sent in a request (docs/data-feed.md "Theta Data in Massive's place")
THETADATA_API_KEY=

# Massive flat files (S3) — a later step; nothing reads these yet. The endpoint is https://files.massive.com and the
# bucket flatfiles.
MASSIVE_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
MASSIVE_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
MASSIVE_S3_ENDPOINT=
MASSIVE_S3_BUCKET=

# The field's recorder on its own (npm run feed:recorder; docs/data-feed.md "The recorder's home"): the names it records
# whatever the tabs, its port, and the address a dev server reads the field from. Blank, the dev server reads the
# recorder at http://127.0.0.1:5190 (RECORDER_PORT's default) and records nothing itself while one answers there — so a
# restart of the app or the dev server never cuts a session; a port that refuses falls back to the dev server's own
# recorder. `off` makes the dev server record on its own regardless.
RECORD_NAMES=SPY,QQQ,IWM
RECORDER_PORT=5190
FEED_RECORDER_URL=

# The backfill job on the always-on recorder (server/recorderMain.ts): every session from this date to the session
# before today, oldest first, for BACKFILL_NAMES (the recorded names but the indices by default)
# BACKFILL_FROM=2025-04-01
# BACKFILL_NAMES=SPY,QQQ

# The history downloader (npm run theta:history, scripts/theta-history; scripts/theta-history.cmd keeps it running —
# docs/data-feed.md "The Theta history"). It reads the Theta Terminal already CONNECTED on this machine at
# 127.0.0.1:25503 and never starts or signs into one. Blank is the default named beside each.
# HISTORY_ROOT=.feed-cache/history          where the raw rows go (gzipped NDJSON, a folder a ticker, a folder a day)
# HISTORY_TICKERS=                          daily and minute candles for these (every name in the app, SPY, QQQ, IWM, DIA)
# HISTORY_CHAIN_ROOTS=SPY,QQQ,SPX,SPXW      the option chains: contracts, open interest and minute quotes a day
# HISTORY_NBBO=SPY,QQQ                      one-minute NBBO (bid, ask, top-of-book sizes)
# HISTORY_INDICES=SPX,NDX,RUT,VIX           the index price series a minute, their candles
# HISTORY_WINDOW_DAYS=60                    a chain's expirations within this many calendar days
# HISTORY_MONEYNESS=0.15                    a chain's strikes within this share of the day's range
# HISTORY_IN_SESSION_CONCURRENCY=3          requests in flight in market hours (the recorder keeps the rest of Theta's 8)
# HISTORY_CONCURRENCY=8                     requests in flight outside them
# HISTORY_REPORT_AFTER=5                    sessions before report.md (GB and minutes a session, the projection, free disk)
# HISTORY_SESSIONS=                         a cap on the sessions walked (a test); HISTORY_FROM=YYYY-MM-DD a floor date
# HISTORY_RETRY_DENIED=1                    ask again what a plan refused (471) last time
# HISTORY_FORCE=1                           go on past a projection larger than the free disk
# HISTORY_RATES=auto                        `none` skips the rate series (Theta's TREASURY_M3, else FRED's DTB3)
# The rebuild (npm run theta:rebuild -- SPY QQQ SPX [--days N] [--again]) reads HISTORY_ROOT and writes beside the
# field: FIELD_ROOT=.feed-cache/field
